.TH TUI_HEADER_INIT 3 2026-11-09 "libtuikit 0.8" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_header_init, tui_header_set_left, tui_header_set_right,
tui_header_set_notice, tui_header_set_warning, tui_header_clear_warning,
tui_header_notice, tui_header_warning_active, tui_header_handle,
tui_header_render, tui_header_format \-
the header bar: view, program name and a notice area
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/header.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_header_init(tui_header *" h );
.BI "void tui_header_set_left(tui_header *" h ", const char *" text );
.BI "void tui_header_set_right(tui_header *" h ", const char *" text );
.BI "void tui_header_set_notice(tui_header *" h ", const char *" text ", tui_style " style );
.BI "void tui_header_set_warning(tui_header *" h ", const char *" text );
.BI "void tui_header_clear_warning(tui_header *" h );
.BI "const char *tui_header_notice(const tui_header *" h );
.BI "int  tui_header_warning_active(const tui_header *" h );
.BI "tui_header_result tui_header_handle(tui_header *" h ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_header_render(tui_header *" h ", tui_canvas " c );
.BI "int  tui_header_format(const tui_header *" h ", int " cols ", char *" out ", size_t " outsz );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tui_header
is the top bar of a program, drawn on the first row of a canvas in the scheme's
header role.
It holds the view (and at most one count or filter) on the left, the program's
name on the right, and between them a notice area for messages and standing
warnings; the key hints stay on the bottom line,
.BR tui_statusline_init (3).
.PP
.BR tui_header_init ()
makes an empty bar; the struct must not be copied.
.BR tui_header_set_left ()
and
.BR tui_header_set_right ()
set the two texts (controls become spaces; NULL or "" clears).
.PP
.BR tui_header_set_notice ()
shows a plain notice in
.IR style ,
.BR TUI_STYLE_OK ", " TUI_STYLE_ERROR ", " TUI_STYLE_PROGRESS
or the default; the style's colour becomes the notice's background and its
attributes are added, so no new colour is used.
A plain notice is cleared by the next key or paste that reaches
.BR tui_header_handle ()
(it returns
.BR TUI_HEADER_CHANGED ;
a resize and every other event are
.BR TUI_HEADER_IGNORED ).
.PP
.BR tui_header_set_warning ()
shows a standing warning in the error role.
It stays across keys until
.BR tui_header_clear_warning ()
or until another warning is set.
It replaces a plain notice that shows, and a plain notice set while a warning
stands is not shown.
.BR tui_header_notice ()
gives the text that shows ("" when none) and
.BR tui_header_warning_active ()
tells whether it is a warning.
.PP
When the row is too narrow, the left text is cut first (with an ellipsis, then
dropped), then the notice; the name is never cut unless it alone is wider than
the row.
.BR tui_header_render ()
draws the bar over the whole width of the canvas.
.BR tui_header_format ()
writes the same row as plain text for
.I cols
columns, without trailing blanks; it returns the length, or \-1 when
.I outsz
was too small (the text is then cut at a character).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libtuikit (7),
.BR tui_statusline_init (3),
.BR tui_scheme_style (3)
